{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The build script looks correct to me. Let me check what the verifier actually computed. The issue might be that I used a different population filter in my obligation. Let me look at what I declared:\n\nIn my obligation, I declared:\n```\n\"population\": \"source.filter(source.state_name != 'Puerto Rico').filter(source.state_name != 'Virgin Islands')\",\n\"expression\": \"source.aggregate(total=source.farmers_markets.sum()).select('total')\",\n\"predicate\": {\"select\": \"total\"}\n```\n\nBut wait, I think I misunderstood what the `population` field is for. According to the instructions, `population` is \"Restriction of the alias the witness ranges over — chained filters only (`source.filter(a).filter(b)`; no `&`/`|`, joins, or limits).\"\n\nHowever, for an ungrounded scalar on the farmers_markets alias that's a bare cell, I should just use `predicate.select` without an expression. But here I need to compute an aggregate. So I need to provide `expression`. The issue is that the `population` might not be applied to the expression correctly.\n\nLet me re-read the instructions more carefully. It says:\n\"An ungrounded scalar whose value is a bare cell of the alias needs only `predicate.select` — the checker synthesizes the selection; give it `expression` (the full expression whose cell is the value, e.g. `source.aggregate(total=source.n.sum())`) only when the cell must be computed.\"\n\nSo I need to provide the full expression including the filters. Let me correct my obligation. But wait, maybe the issue is different. Let me look at what the verifier actually says. It said:\n\n```\n✗ total_markets   7942 ⟶ 7944\n```\n\nSo when it re-ran the witness with the population filter I specified, it got 7944, not 7942. That means my filter isn't working right OR the data I'm seeing is different somehow. \nTerritories excluded should just be Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands — DC isn't a territory so it stays in. State abbreviations PR and VI confirm these are the ones to drop. My filter logic seems right, so maybe there's a subtle data issue like whitespace in the state names. I should try verifying without the population field to isolate the problem.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Let me fix my verification - I'll provide the correct expression that includes the filters:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_014F5faR8Q6imC6AHd9aVc5M","name":"xorq_verify","arguments":{"request":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","obligations":[{"id":"total_markets","kind":"scalar","on":"farmers_markets","surface":"7942","expression":"source.filter(source.state_name != 'Puerto Rico').filter(source.state_name != 'Virgin Islands').aggregate(total=source.farmers_markets.sum()).select('total')","predicate":{"select":"total"},"value_type":{"kind":"int"}},{"id":"us_population_2025","kind":"scalar","on":"census_population","surface":"341784857","population":"source.filter(source.NAME == 'United States')","predicate":{"select":"POPESTIMATE2025"},"value_type":{"kind":"int"}},{"id":"markets_per_100k","kind":"scalar","on":"markets_per_capita","surface":"2.3237","predicate":{"select":"markets_per_100k"},"value_type":{"kind":"decimal","tolerance":"0.00005"}}],"reply_values":["7942","341784857","2.3237"]}}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":947,"cacheRead":23417,"cacheWrite":757,"totalTokens":25134,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.0047350000000000005,"cacheRead":0.0023417000000000004,"cacheWrite":0.00094625,"total":0.00803595},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":582},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912831109,"responseId":"msg_011Ce75GhpirivmAkTq1vo2X","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_014F5faR8Q6imC6AHd9aVc5M","toolName":"xorq_verify","content":[{"type":"text","text":" ✅ VERIFIED   3 obligations  ·  catalog db0916…\n   ✓ total_markets   7942 ⟶ 7942\n 